  "description": "Breeze is a low step-through cargo electric bike with 20-inch fat tires, a 750W Bafang motor and one 48V 20Ah LG-cell battery. An upright riding position, front suspension and included rear rack support commuting, shopping trips and everyday leisure rides.\n\nHow does a low step-through frame help at stops?\n\nBreeze has an 18.5-inch standover height, leaving an open space for mounting and dismounting. The step-through electric bike suits rides with frequent stops, from neighborhood trips to shopping runs, with a saddle that adjusts to your riding position.\n\nWhat makes a 20-inch fat tire ebike different?\n\nBreeze pairs 20-inch wheels with 4-inch-wide Kenda fat tires for a smaller-wheel riding format. The wide tires and front suspension cushion uneven pavement and recreational gravel routes, giving this electric bicycle everyday versatility beyond a smooth cycle path.\n\nHow does 750W power help with commuting?\n\nThe 750W Bafang rear hub motor adds assistance for starts, hills and everyday travel. Five pedal-assist levels let you choose how much help you want, while Shimano 7-speed gearing adjusts your pedaling rhythm. A thumb throttle provides assistance without pedaling.\n\nWhat helps you see and be seen after dusk?\n\nA 45-lux headlight illuminates the route ahead, while the integrated rear light and reflective tire details improve visibility when light is limited. Logan hydraulic disc brakes add controlled braking to this commuter electric bike on changing everyday routes.\n\nWhat does the single 20Ah battery offer?\n\nOne 48V 20Ah LG-cell battery stores 960Wh of energy inside the frame. Breeze's current single-battery layout keeps the rear rack available for daily essentials, bringing electric assistance to work commutes, leisure rides and trips across town.\n\nCan a cargo electric bicycle carry daily essentials?\n\nBreeze includes a rear rack and full fenders for shopping trips and commuting. Fit a compatible basket or bag for groceries and work items. Its 350 lb total payload covers the rider, cargo and accessories, rather than the rear rack alone.",
